{
  "protocolVersion": "2025-11-25",
  "capabilities": {
    "tools": {}
  },
  "serverInfo": {
    "name": "dbmcp",
    "title": "dbmcp",
    "version": "[version]",
    "description": "The privacy first MCP server for SQL databases.",
    "websiteUrl": "https://dbmcp.haymon.ai"
  },
  "instructions": "## Workflow\n\n1. Call `objects` to discover tables, views, materialized views, triggers, functions, and procedures (in the `public` schema) before writing SQL. Pass `kind` to pick the object kind (default `table`), `search` to filter by name, and `detail: \"full\"` for columns, constraints, indexes, and definitions.\n2. Use `read` for read-only SQL (SELECT, SHOW, EXPLAIN).\n3. Use `write` for data and schema changes (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, CREATE, ALTER, DROP).\n4. Use `explain` to analyze query execution plans and diagnose slow queries.\n\nTools default to the active database.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- This server is scoped to a single configured database; `objects` does not offer `kind: \"database\"`.\n- The `write` tool is hidden when read-only mode is active.\n- Multi-statement queries are not supported. Send one statement per request.\n"
}
